# Cursor execution: thin adapter

Read root [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md), the commissioned Change's `CHANGE.md`/`TASKS.md`, and the [canonical parent policy](../../.agents/references/bounded-parent-orchestration.md); **those own the rules**. Do not duplicate lifecycle/branch/batch policy here.

**Before first implementation edit:** on a dedicated `change/<id>-<slug>` branch based on the packet's real integration target, run `node scripts/repo-tools/change-branch-guard.mjs --change <ID> --target <reference-branch>`. If the target moved, reconcile it rather than resetting. A **separate linked worktree is mandatory per commissioned Change**, even if no other chat is active. Never switch the user's primary checkout. No worktree per T-ID. Run the branch guard inside the dedicated worktree.

**Parent:** default Composer Standard; dispatch one small PLANNER-READY T-ID at a time (two only for disjoint source owners). Checkpoint each 2–5 tasks and continue the **same** owner-commissioned Change through its true acceptance/closure. Do not auto-start another Change. The designated integration owner serializes shared-file merges when several Change chats operate concurrently.

**Child:** assigned `DEPTH=VERIFY|PATCH|INVESTIGATE`, one T-ID, a few named source anchors, specific patch/normal/negative test and short receipt. No agent swarms, broad research, unrelated refactors, expensive-model self-upgrades, full suite per child, or shared-checkout commits. Verify only what the task needs. If a true architecture/permission/transaction contradiction appears, return file:symbol, failing assumption and reproducer to parent/ChatGPT. Ordinary unrelated local errors may be fixed with bounded diagnosis; do not loop on the same unexplained failure.

**Evidence:** report actual edits, tests/results, negative case, remaining blocker and spend. Never treat unrun checks as passed; no paid model calls or destructive resources without explicit approval. For repo-folder work consult [structure map](../../REPOSITORY-STRUCTURE.md).
